Package: topologyR
Type: Package
Title: Topological Connectivity Analysis for Numeric Data
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "José Mauricio", family = "Gómez Julián",
           email = "isadore.nabi@pm.me", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Builds topologies on the vertex set of a graph from the
    closed neighbourhoods of its vertices, a closed-neighbourhood variant of
    the construction of Nada, El Atik and Atef (2018) <doi:10.1002/mma.4726>,
    and computes their connected components exactly through the
    specialization preorder, without enumerating the topology. For time
    series it builds the horizontal and natural visibility graphs (Luque et
    al., 2009, <doi:10.1103/PhysRevE.80.046103>; Lacasa et al., 2008,
    <doi:10.1073/pnas.0709247105>) at equally or unequally spaced instants,
    deciding the natural criterion exactly under IEEE 754 double
    arithmetic, and from their
    directed versions the forward and backward topologies, a bitopological
    space in the sense of Kelly (1963) <doi:10.1112/plms/s3-13.1.71>,
    together with the Alexandrov topology of reachability. Reading a series
    backwards, with its instants reflected, exchanges the two topologies, so
    the difference of their numbers of components changes sign.
